A1 L1: Every dug depth D1..D4 draws its own wall-face height (RM_WallFaceMath.NorthByDrop strictly rising; SelfTest WallFaces_every_depth_differs), liquid covers the foot of the wall (ExposedDrop shrinks by the fill: a 4-deep cut with 3 notches of water shows a 1-notch face)
A2 L1: RM_Spikes, RM_Ladder and RM_LadderRaised ship bespoke PNGs (no magenta) and no FlowWorks def points at Things/Building/Security/TrapSpikeArmed.
A3 L3: In a frame, D1..D4 read as visibly different depths and a superdeep cell reads as a hole, not a building (pit_depth_ladder_legible, pit_reads_as_hole, never_reads_as_building)
A4 L3: In a frame, some amount of spike shows at the bottom of a spiked D=4 cell (spikes_read_distinct).
A5 L4: The owner reviews the wall faces, spikes and ladder in game and keeps them.
